IF STATEMENTS

Theyre one of the simplest advanced condition statements, used to execute a certain fuction if a condition(s) is met.

Its syntax is as follows:

if (your condition
{
  //whatever happens if its met
}
else (or else if)*
{
  //whatever happens if the secondary condition (elseif) is met OR what happens if the original or secondary conditions arent met.
}

  *The statement still works even without any Else or ElseIf appendages. You do not need to add them every single time!

EX:

  if (isCreepyClown == False)
  {
    Console.WriteLine("I like this guy!");
  }
  else
  {
    Console.WriteLine("AAAH!");
  }

This was one of the first things I learned to do in programming, its an evergreen statement that always helps out. I figured out how to imagine it in my head better when I
started using flowcharts and messing around with a compiler. As standardized and professional as one must normally be with code, messing around is never bad when not important! Maybe you'll understand a concept better
when you're not chained down by responsability, who knows! Just don't let writing lousy or silly code become a habit!
